1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,400
The nearest star beyond the Sun is about 40 trillion km away.

2
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:09,633
And a hydrogen atom weighs this much, in grams.

3
00:00:09,633 --> 00:00:12,633
Numbers like these are hard to read…

4
00:00:12,633 --> 00:00:16,167
…so scientists use scientific notation.

5
00:00:16,167 --> 00:00:21,767
A number from 1 up to 10, times a power of 10.

6
00:00:21,767 --> 00:00:25,667
The exponent n is an integer.

7
00:00:25,667 --> 00:00:31,667
4 × 10¹³: move the point 13 places right.

8
00:00:31,667 --> 00:00:33,800
Forty trillion.

9
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:37,233
A negative exponent moves the point left…

10
00:00:37,233 --> 00:00:42,300
…24 places for the hydrogen atom.

11
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:44,500
Positive exponent: a big number.

12
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:48,033
Negative exponent: a tiny one.

13
00:00:48,033 --> 00:00:50,233
One digit before the point,

14
00:00:50,233 --> 00:00:54,800
times a power of 10.
